                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 52.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Hall</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 10,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Hall is informed that, while the United States Government is prepared to use
                    its influence in averting a conflict and to promote peace, and deems advisable a
                    voluntary combination of interests of the Central American States, no display of
                    force on the part of any one or more States to coerce the others can be
                    countenanced.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
